## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Năm: Câu hỏi phỏng vấn

### 16:30–16:40 · Shadowing

### 16:40–16:55 · Trả lời có ghi âm

**Câu hỏi tuần này:** *"How do you use AI in your workflow?"*

Câu này gần như chắc chắn được hỏi trong năm 2026, và đa số ứng viên trả lời rất nông — *"tôi dùng Copilot, nó giúp code nhanh hơn."* Đây là cơ hội nổi bật.

> *"I treat it as a very fast, very confident junior. It writes code that compiles, and it doesn't know the constraints of my project unless I tell it.*
> *So two things changed how I work. First, I write a short spec before I generate anything — behaviour, constraints, what's out of scope, and acceptance criteria. Then the spec is both the input and the thing I check against, instead of eyeballing the output and deciding it looks fine.*
> *Second, I keep a rules file in the repo so it follows the project's conventions rather than inventing its own.*
> *On review — I never accept a diff I haven't read line by line. I've got a checklist of what it gets wrong most: swallowed errors, missing effect cleanup, stale closures, and trusting external data because the type says it's a string.*
> *The category I watch hardest is business logic that reads correctly and is wrong. Off-by-one on a date range, or a timezone assumption. That code passes review because it looks right — only a test catches it. Which is one more reason I write the test myself and let it write the implementation, rather than the other way round."*

### 16:55–17:00 · 5 từ mới

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `eyeball` (v) | nhìn lướt qua áng chừng | *Instead of eyeballing the output.* |
| `swallow an error` | nuốt lỗi, giấu lỗi | *Swallowed errors are the most common.* |
| `stale closure` | closure giữ giá trị cũ | *Stale closures are hard to spot.* |
| `the other way round` | ngược lại | *Rather than the other way round.* |
| `low bar` | tiêu chuẩn thấp | *It compiles. That's a low bar.* |

